// test-error
// test-adr: 030
// #1582, cross-file: write-sibling-consumer.cnx WRITES a variable declared in
// write-sibling-source.cnx without including it.
//
// Paired with undeclared-write-sibling-consumer-first.test.cnx -- same two
// sources, opposite include order, and the two must produce the IDENTICAL
// diagnostic set. `knownVariables` is assembled incrementally and is
// order-sensitive, which is what made #1430 flip a diagnostic on and off by
// swapping two `#include` lines. The pair asserts that, rather than a comment
// anyone has to trust.
//
// Both halves carry the `-first` suffix on purpose: scripts/__tests__/
// order-pair-fixtures.test.ts treats that name as a promise of a pair and
// fails a directory holding a lone half.
#include <write-sibling-source.cnx>
#include <write-sibling-consumer.cnx>

u32 main() {
    return 0;
}
